# expected.carrier.log
# attestation: spec-derived from IEEE 1516.1-2010 references below
# Cross-check status: NOT CROSS-CHECKED — fixture uses >2 federates; exceeds the free-edition federate cap of the reference RTI used for local cross-checks. Independently verifiable against any DLC-conformant RTI via the PRTI_HOME-gated harness. See docs/PITCH_PARITY.md.
# canonicalization: cppsdk/tests/dlc/conformance/_harness/normalize.py
# spec-cites: see README.md
# Per IEEE 1516.1-2010 §4.2, §4.9, §6.8, §7.2, §4.10:
# parity-CD golden fix (spec-wins): the carrier must §7.2-divest
# Position for the §7.9 race to have a winner — acquisitionIfAvailable
# only acquires UNOWNED attributes and never solicits release from an
# owner, so the M31 scenario (carrier holds Position throughout) made
# the bob-wins golden unreachable under any compliant RTI.
CARRIER: CONNECT
CARRIER: JOIN
CARRIER: REGISTER name=car-race handle=<H>
CARRIER: UNCONDITIONAL_DIVEST attrs=[Position]
CARRIER: RESIGN
